{"agent":"fix-export-bugs-test","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new expression `\"\" if getattr(b, \"scope\", \"project\") in (\"\", \"project\") else str(b.scope)` regresses the handling of a falsy-but-present scope value. The original line was `str(getattr(b, \"scope\", \"\") or \"\")`, whose `or \"\"` collapsed `None` (and any other falsy value) to the empty string. Now, when `b.scope` exists but is `None` — e.g. a bug persisted with a JSON `null` scope and loaded into the model — `getattr(...)` returns `None`, which is not in `(\"\", \"project\")`, so the `else` branch runs and `str(None)` yields the literal string `\"None\"`. The rendered BUGS.md line then carries a bogus `[None]` tag instead of no tag, which is both incorrect output and inconsistent with the stated goal (only a non-default scope should render). Passing a bug record with `scope=None` through this exporter demonstrates it: expected `\"\"`, actual `\"None\"`. The fix is to normalize None as well, e.g. `\"\" if getattr(b, \"scope\", \"project\") in (\"\", None, \"project\") else str(b.scope)`.","digest":"dd09d242b140c1fe","location":"ddflow/services/export/kind_bugs.py:58","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/export/kind_bugs.py:58"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_chars":1608,"diff_sha":"97dc1bc36cd3419e8cc00d7afa2a1d938d59620e82e909cfd1d2ebef9f6fd8c6","diff_source":"main..HEAD + working tree in /home/delian/src/.ddflow-worktrees/B-fix-export-bugs-default-scope","elapsed_s":14.3,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","reason":"","reviewed":[1],"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/export/kind_bugs.py:58"],"unreviewed":[]},"gate":"critic","reason":"1 finding(s)"},"id":"e7ebc8702b674244ef424dec1","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":10581,"schema":1,"subject":"B-fix-export-bugs-default-scope","ts":"2026-10-02T16:03:01.503039Z"}
{"agent":"fix-export-bugs-test","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new expression drops the falsy/`None` guard that the old code had. `getattr(b, \"scope\", \"\") or \"\"` mapped a missing, empty, **or `None`** scope to `\"\"`; the replacement maps only the literal values `\"\"` and `\"project\"` to `\"\"`, and sends everything else through `str(b.scope)`. So for a bug whose `scope` attribute exists but holds `None` (a plausible case for records loaded from an older store that predates the scope field, which is exactly the migration the surrounding `\"\"\" until B-bug-scope-event\"` comment alludes to), `getattr(b, \"scope\", \"project\")` returns `None`, `None in (\"\", \"project\")` is `False`, and the else-branch produces `str(None) == \"None\"`. The exported record's `scope` becomes the truthy string `\"None\"` instead of empty, so BUGS.md renders a bogus `[None]` scope tag on every such line — the opposite of the stated intent. Note the test added in the diff only covers `\"project\"` and `\"ddflow\"`, so it does not exercise this path. Fix by normalizing the value first, e.g. `s = getattr(b, \"scope\", None) or \"\"` then `\"scope\": \"\" if s in (\"\", \"project\") else str(s)`.","digest":"88a09d90baae2f5b","location":"ddflow/services/export/kind_bugs.py:58","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/export/kind_bugs.py:58"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_chars":1608,"diff_sha":"97dc1bc36cd3419e8cc00d7afa2a1d938d59620e82e909cfd1d2ebef9f6fd8c6","diff_source":"main..HEAD + working tree in /home/delian/src/.ddflow-worktrees/B-fix-export-bugs-default-scope","elapsed_s":16.0,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","reason":"","reviewed":[1],"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/export/kind_bugs.py:58"],"unreviewed":[]},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"1 finding(s)"},"id":"e7ea1e73c4c10f66da50534b7","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":10582,"schema":1,"subject":"B-fix-export-bugs-default-scope","ts":"2026-10-02T16:03:03.198528Z"}
